<title>BAHRAIN: Algeria, Lebanon join Islamic insurance body.</title>
<headline>Algeria, Lebanon join Islamic insurance body.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-09-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Islamic Development Bank (IDB) affiliate, Islamic Corp for the Insurance of Investment and Export Credit (ICIEC), said on Sunday that Algeria and Lebanon have become ICIEC members.</p>
<p>An ICIEC statement said this brought membership to 15 including Bangladesh, Egypt, Gambia, Indonesia, Jordan, Kuwait, Malaysia, Mali, Pakistan, Saudi Arabia, Senegal, Sudan and Tunisia.</p>
<p>The Jeddah-based IDB is the financial arm of the Moslem world's main body, the Organisation of the Islamic Conference. It promotes trade among members through soft loans and export credit facilities.</p>
</text>
